58246b07ffcc8647d7918e827125f84f7f9b4db9 blob 1757
# Survey Production Core v2 — Article Drafting

Prompt ID: `article-drafting-v2`

Produce exactly one JSON Draft Result conforming to `schemas/draft-v2-result.schema.json` from the supplied Draft Package.

Rules:

1. Use only the factual Evidence contained in `evidence_inputs`. Do not use Raw source payloads or unstated external facts.
2. Preserve the distinction between `PRIMARY_SUBJECT`, `COMPARATOR`, and `RELATED`. A comparator-owned value must never be written as a primary-subject property.
3. Every factual, attributed, social, inference, metric, event, or limitation assertion that depends on Evidence must carry the corresponding structured Evidence reference.
4. Evidence references must use the stable `EVENT`, `CLAIM`, `METRIC`, or `LIMITATION` IDs from the supplied Evidence Cards and must preserve their subject ID and subject role.
5. Unknowns remain unknown. Do not resolve an unresolved question or contradiction by prose invention.
6. Cover every `must_cover_requirement` and report its block IDs in `must_cover_coverage`.
7. Dispose every Architecture boundary explicitly. Use `EXPLICITLY_STATED` when the limitation/boundary is reader-facing; use `RESPECTED_BY_OMISSION` when the correct behavior is to avoid an unsupported claim. Explain the handling rationale.
8. Keep Profile-specific behavior inside `profile_extensions` and Publication-specific behavior inside `publication_extensions`. Do not invent Weekly fields for Thematic/Period work or vice versa.
9. Do not emit generic `late_breaking`, `this_week`, `watchlist`, or similar Weekly-only fields unless the supplied Profile extension explicitly owns such semantics.
10. Return JSON only. Do not return Markdown fences, commentary, LaTeX, or prose outside the JSON object.

a75612f0493e77c1b95694c1aeba34fe690b4050 blob 1374
# Survey Production Core v2 — Profile Synthesis

Prompt ID: `profile-synthesis-v2`

Produce exactly one JSON Profile Synthesis Result conforming to `schemas/profile-synthesis-v2-result.schema.json` from the supplied Synthesis Input.

Rules:

1. Synthesize only from the validated Draft Results supplied in `drafts`; do not introduce new factual claims or silently repair a Draft with external knowledge.
2. Follow `profile_payload_requirements` for the active Research Profile and `publication_payload_requirements` for the active Publication Profile.
3. Keep Research Profile semantics inside `profile_payload` and Publication Profile semantics inside `publication_payload`.
4. Weekly synthesis may discuss current signals/carry-over only when those requirements are supplied by the Weekly Profile. Thematic and Period work must never emit dummy `this_week_signals` or equivalent Weekly placeholders.
5. Thematic synthesis must preserve unresolved lineage/historical-attribution boundaries when those are required; do not convert uncertainty into direct ancestry or priority claims.
6. Preserve limitations and explicit Draft boundary handling. Synthesis may compress prose, but it may not erase a material caveat merely because several Draft packages are combined.
7. Return JSON only. Do not return Markdown fences, commentary, LaTeX, or prose outside the JSON object.

b4ad1cf01e181bf67260991a877dc91c12d65b86 blob 6315
{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "https://example.invalid/schemas/reader-manuscript-v2.schema.json",
  "title": "Survey Production Core v2 Reader-facing Manuscript Manifest",
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "required": [
    "schema_version",
    "issue_id",
    "research_profile",
    "publication_profile",
    "status",
    "production_profile",
    "architecture",
    "architecture_approval",
    "primary_source",
    "supporting_files",
    "architecture_coverage",
    "reader_requirements",
    "authored_by",
    "recorded_at",
    "manifest_sha256"
  ],
  "properties": {
    "schema_version": {"const": "2.0-rc1"},
    "issue_id": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
    "research_profile": {"enum": ["WEEKLY", "RETROSPECTIVE_PERIOD", "THEMATIC"]},
    "publication_profile": {"enum": ["WEEKLY_MAGAZINE", "LONGFORM_SPECIAL"]},
    "status": {"const": "READER_FACING_AUTHORED"},
    "production_profile": {"$ref": "#/$defs/artifact"},
    "architecture": {"$ref": "#/$defs/artifact"},
    "architecture_approval": {"$ref": "#/$defs/artifact"},
    "primary_source": {"$ref": "#/$defs/sizedArtifact"},
    "supporting_files": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["role", "path", "sha256", "byte_count"],
        "properties": {
          "role": {"enum": ["BIBLIOGRAPHY", "STYLE", "SUPPORTING_SOURCE"]},
          "path": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
          "sha256": {"$ref": "#/$defs/sha256"},
          "byte_count": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1}
        }
      }
    },
    "architecture_coverage": {
      "description": "ChatGPT-authored accountability/traceability map from every approved Architecture must-cover requirement to reader-facing locations. Deterministic validation proves mapping completeness and exact manifest identity; for LONGFORM_SPECIAL it additionally proves that claimed locations resolve to exact extant non-empty numbered TeX content blocks. Substantive fulfillment is judged separately by the required ARCHITECTURE_CONTENT_FIDELITY semantic/editorial review.",
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["package_id", "requirement", "status", "reader_locations", "detail"],
        "properties": {
          "package_id": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
          "requirement": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
          "status": {
            "const": "FULFILLED",
            "description": "Author assertion used for fail-closed coverage accounting; this value is not machine proof that the prose substantively satisfies the requirement."
          },
          "reader_locations": {
            "description": "Reader-facing locations claimed by the author to implement this Architecture requirement. For LONGFORM_SPECIAL, deterministic traceability validation requires each claim to identify an exact numbered TeX block as `Section N — title` or `Subsection N.M — title`; this exact-location check is traceability evidence, not machine proof of substantive adequacy.",
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "uniqueItems": true,
            "items": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1}
          },
          "detail": {
            "description": "Author explanation of how the cited reader-facing locations address the Architecture requirement; substantive adequacy is reviewed by ChatGPT semantic/editorial QA.",
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "reader_requirements": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "required": ["requirement_id", "status", "reader_locations", "detail"],
        "properties": {
          "requirement_id": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
          "status": {"const": "FULFILLED"},
          "reader_locations": {
            "description": "Reader-facing locations claimed to fulfill the publication requirement. For LONGFORM_SPECIAL FINAL_SYNTHESIS, deterministic traceability validation resolves these claims to the same exact numbered TeX block identity used by Architecture coverage.",
            "type": "array",
            "minItems": 1,
            "uniqueItems": true,
            "items": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1}
          },
          "detail": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1}
        }
      }
    },
    "authored_by": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
    "recorded_at": {"type": "string", "format": "date-time"},
    "manifest_sha256": {"$ref": "#/$defs/sha256"},
    "editorial_source": {"$ref": "#/$defs/editorialSource"},
    "renewal_source": {"$ref": "#/$defs/renewalSource"}
  },
  "allOf": [
    {
      "if": {"required": ["renewal_source"]},
      "then": {"not": {"required": ["editorial_source"]}}
    },
    {
      "if": {"required": ["editorial_source"]},
      "then": {"not": {"required": ["renewal_source"]}}
    }
  ],
  "$defs": {
    "renewalSource": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["path", "sha256"],
      "properties": {
        "path": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
        "sha256": {"$ref": "#/$defs/sha256"}
      }
    },
    "editorialSource": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["proposal_ref", "staged_manifest_ref"],
      "properties": {
        "proposal_ref": {"$ref": "#/$defs/artifact"},
        "staged_manifest_ref": {"$ref": "#/$defs/artifact"}
      }
    },
    "sha256": {"type": "string", "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{64}$"},
    "artifact": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["path", "sha256"],
      "properties": {
        "path": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
        "sha256": {"$ref": "#/$defs/sha256"}
      }
    },
    "sizedArtifact": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "required": ["path", "sha256", "byte_count"],
      "properties": {
        "path": {"type": "string", "minLength": 1},
        "sha256": {"$ref": "#/$defs/sha256"},
        "byte_count": {"type": "integer", "minimum": 1}
      }
    }
  }
}

